{"reply":"You could put it this way:

> I’m torn between admitting things immediately and trying to repair them quietly. One part of me values honesty; another is afraid that being seen making a mistake will change how people see me. Tonight, those impulses feel less like a single conflict and more like two different selves arguing over what would keep me safe.

Or, more simply: **“I want to be honest, but I also want to protect myself from being judged—and tonight those wants feel like they belong to two different people.”**","memory":{"kind":"no_memory_candidate","reason_code":"automatic_capture_disabled"}}
